            <div xml:id="d309-a2">

                <pb facs="0511" n="441" xml:id="pg441"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Señor S. Lerdo de Tejada to Mr. Otterbourg</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of Foreign Relations,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 24, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I had the honor to receive your note of to-day, informing me that you had
                    received a commission from your government naming you envoy extraordinary and
                    minister plenipotentiary of the United States of America near the government of
                    the republic of Mexico.</p>
                <p>It will be gratifying to the President of the republic to receive you in your
                    character of representative of the United States of America; and I hope that you
                    will communicate to me that you are prepared to present to him your credentials,
                    in order that he may designate the day that he may be able to receive you. I
                    avail myself of this occasion, Mr. Minister, to assure you of my very
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marcus Otterbourg,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of
                            the U. S. of America near the government of the United Mexican
                            States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
